The Mulick in these Temples of Venus is perform'd by Organs, not out of Respect to the Deity that is worship'd in them, but the frugality of the Owners, whose Business it is to procure as much found for as little Money as they can, and the Policy of the Government, who endeavours as little as is possible, to encourage the Breed of Pipers and Scrapers. All Sea-faring Men, especially the Dutch, are like the Element they belong to, much given to loudness and roaring, and the Noise of half a dozen of them, when they call themselves Merry, is sufficient to drown twice the number of Flutes or Violins;

